1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,255
You wake up, and your phone is full

2
00:00:02,275 --> 00:00:04,510
of messages nobody sent.

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:05,912
Your boss typed,

4
00:00:06,003 --> 00:00:07,211
<i>“You're fired.”</i>

5
00:00:07,381 --> 00:00:08,591
Then deleted it.

6
00:00:08,611 --> 00:00:09,992
Your mum typed,

7
00:00:10,082 --> 00:00:11,649
<i>“Are you eating properly?”</i>

8
00:00:11,819 --> 00:00:13,369
Eleven times.

9
00:00:13,649 --> 00:00:16,179
And at three a.m., your best friend

10
00:00:16,199 --> 00:00:17,379
typed three words…

11
00:00:17,399 --> 00:00:18,816
and held backspace.

12
00:00:19,456 --> 00:00:20,629
<i>“I'm not okay.”</i>

13
00:00:21,299 --> 00:00:22,559
She never sent it.

14
00:00:22,579 --> 00:00:24,383
You could answer anyway.

15
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:29,713
They look like normal messages.

16
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:31,183
Just grey.

17
00:00:31,203 --> 00:00:32,718
And they flicker, like they're still

18
00:00:32,738 --> 00:00:34,072
deciding.

19
00:00:34,092 --> 00:00:36,272
Everything anyone almost said to you

20
00:00:36,292 --> 00:00:37,567
since midnight.

21
00:00:37,592 --> 00:00:39,167
Two hundred and twelve.

22
00:00:39,187 --> 00:00:40,698
Before breakfast.

23
00:00:40,718 --> 00:00:42,280
The pizza place wrote,

24
00:00:42,369 --> 00:00:43,927
<i>“Sorry about the pineapple.”</i>

25
00:00:44,097 --> 00:00:46,272
Then sent a coupon instead.

26
00:00:46,502 --> 00:00:48,188
The group chat is worse.

27
00:00:48,278 --> 00:00:50,092
<i>“Is he bringing the guitar again?”</i>

28
00:00:50,182 --> 00:00:51,312
<i>“Somebody tell him.”</i>

29
00:00:51,332 --> 00:00:52,069
<i>“Not me.”</i>

30
00:00:52,639 --> 00:00:54,019
Nobody tells you.

31
00:00:54,039 --> 00:00:56,174
Tonight, the guitar stays home.

32
00:00:57,164 --> 00:00:59,418
In the lift, a stranger types,

33
00:00:59,508 --> 00:01:00,713
<i>“I like your hoodie.”</i>

34
00:01:00,883 --> 00:01:02,151
And deletes it.

35
00:01:02,741 --> 00:01:04,905
You stand a little taller anyway.

36
00:01:06,555 --> 00:01:08,956
At work, it turns out to be useful.

37
00:01:09,046 --> 00:01:10,766
<i>“Where is that report?”</i>

38
00:01:10,936 --> 00:01:12,348
Report's on your desk.

39
00:01:12,368 --> 00:01:13,123
I was…

40
00:01:13,143 --> 00:01:14,546
just about to ask.

41
00:01:14,566 --> 00:01:15,689
Lucky guess.

42
00:01:16,679 --> 00:01:18,585
<i>“Could you cover Friday?”</i>

43
00:01:18,605 --> 00:01:19,375
<i>“No.”</i>

44
00:01:19,395 --> 00:01:20,239
<i>“Forget it.”</i>

45
00:01:20,409 --> 00:01:21,906
I can cover Friday.

46
00:01:21,926 --> 00:01:23,079
How did you

47
00:01:23,099 --> 00:01:24,694
You look like a Friday.

48
00:01:24,844 --> 00:01:26,749
By lunch, you're answering questions

49
00:01:26,769 --> 00:01:28,354
nobody asked.

50
00:01:28,374 --> 00:01:30,175
It feels like kindness.

51
00:01:30,265 --> 00:01:32,793
<i>“Should I warn him about the budget?”</i>

52
00:01:32,963 --> 00:01:34,758
Is something wrong with the budget?

53
00:01:34,778 --> 00:01:36,161
Who told you that?

54
00:01:36,711 --> 00:01:39,271
It doesn't feel like kindness to them.

55
00:01:39,291 --> 00:01:41,921
By three, people turn their phones face

56
00:01:41,941 --> 00:01:43,630
down when you walk past.

57
00:01:45,221 --> 00:01:46,788
<i>“Are you eating properly?”</i>

58
00:01:46,958 --> 00:01:47,568
Twelve.

59
00:01:47,588 --> 00:01:48,866
So you call her.

60
00:01:48,886 --> 00:01:49,366
Hello?

61
00:01:49,386 --> 00:01:50,483
Is something wrong?

62
00:01:50,503 --> 00:01:51,353
No, no.

63
00:01:51,393 --> 00:01:52,693
I just had lunch.

64
00:01:52,713 --> 00:01:53,713
A real one.

65
00:01:53,733 --> 00:01:55,257
Vegetables and everything.

66
00:01:55,277 --> 00:01:56,704
Why are you telling me this?

67
00:01:56,724 --> 00:01:58,277
Thought you'd want to know.

68
00:01:58,677 --> 00:01:59,402
I did.

69
00:01:59,442 --> 00:02:00,698
I did want to know.

70
00:02:00,848 --> 00:02:02,328
That one, you got right.

71
00:02:02,348 --> 00:02:03,353
You answered.

72
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:05,082
And she never knew you'd read it.

73
00:02:06,132 --> 00:02:08,312
All afternoon, one message sits at the

74
00:02:08,332 --> 00:02:09,842
top of the pile.

75
00:02:09,862 --> 00:02:11,092
You don't open it.

76
00:02:11,112 --> 00:02:12,319
You don't need to.

77
00:02:13,229 --> 00:02:14,086
Hey, you.

78
00:02:14,106 --> 00:02:14,361
Hey.

79
00:02:14,381 --> 00:02:15,326
How are you?

80
00:02:15,346 --> 00:02:15,751
Fine!

81
00:02:15,771 --> 00:02:16,126
Tired.

82
00:02:16,146 --> 00:02:16,706
You know.

83
00:02:16,726 --> 00:02:17,186
Fine.

84
00:02:17,206 --> 00:02:17,924
How was work?

85
00:02:17,944 --> 00:02:18,554
Weird.

86
00:02:18,574 --> 00:02:20,595
People kept hiding their phones.

87
00:02:20,615 --> 00:02:22,798
Maybe stop reading over their shoulders.

88
00:02:23,198 --> 00:02:23,503
Yeah.

89
00:02:23,523 --> 00:02:24,363
Maybe.

90
00:02:24,913 --> 00:02:26,093
Above her phone.

91
00:02:26,113 --> 00:02:26,763
Grey.

92
00:02:26,783 --> 00:02:27,937
Still flickering.

93
00:02:28,027 --> 00:02:29,200
<i>“I'm not okay.”</i>

94
00:02:29,370 --> 00:02:31,600
You've had the perfect reply ready all

95
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:32,506
day.

96
00:02:32,526 --> 00:02:34,265
You type it under the table.

97
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:35,988
<i>“I know you're not okay.”</i>

98
00:02:36,158 --> 00:02:37,831
Your thumb is on send.

99
00:02:38,521 --> 00:02:39,526
She didn't send it.

100
00:02:39,546 --> 00:02:40,576
That was a decision.

101
00:02:40,596 --> 00:02:41,525
Hers.

102
00:02:42,115 --> 00:02:43,900
You hold backspace.

103
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:46,125
Now there are two unsent messages at

104
00:02:46,145 --> 00:02:47,073
this table.

105
00:02:47,682 --> 00:02:49,435
Want to split a cinnamon roll?

106
00:02:49,455 --> 00:02:50,020
Yeah.

107
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:50,830
Okay.

108
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,435
You talk about nothing.

109
00:02:52,455 --> 00:02:54,019
Twenty minutes of nothing.

110
00:02:54,729 --> 00:02:56,091
Can I tell you something?

111
00:02:56,111 --> 00:02:57,149
Always.

112
00:02:57,849 --> 00:02:59,025
I'm not okay.

113
00:02:59,875 --> 00:03:00,905
Three words.

114
00:03:00,925 --> 00:03:02,055
Out loud.

115
00:03:02,075 --> 00:03:05,026
Sixteen hours late, and exactly on time.

116
00:03:05,046 --> 00:03:06,066
I'm here.

117
00:03:06,466 --> 00:03:07,331
I didn't get it.

118
00:03:07,351 --> 00:03:08,506
The second interview.

119
00:03:08,526 --> 00:03:10,235
I've been saying fine for a week.

120
00:03:10,255 --> 00:03:12,204
That's a long time to say fine.

121
00:03:12,224 --> 00:03:13,962
It's a very flexible word.

122
00:03:14,712 --> 00:03:16,155
You don't say you knew.

123
00:03:18,045 --> 00:03:20,275
On the way home, your phone buzzes.

124
00:03:20,295 --> 00:03:21,903
A real one, this time.

125
00:03:21,923 --> 00:03:23,427
Thank you for not asking.

126
00:03:25,877 --> 00:03:27,277
Would you read them?
